# nvn/draw: every dropped draw counted by reason, the game's own draw records counted, stretches of frames that
# encoded no draw logged with their causes; DM_METAL_HUD through the game layer's developerHUDProperties
#
# Why: South Park: The Fractured But Whole (01008F2005154000), iPhone 15 Pro, session pid 7174 of 2026-11-22 (~170 s). The picture held, flashed image / black, then jumped
#   about 2 s ahead while the game and its audio ran on. Presents stayed at 30 Hz throughout. Slow-frame rows show frames with @draws=0 over 10 passes
#   (@rt_load_mb 42, all unwritten) around t = 92.5, 101.9-103.7, 106.1-107.0, 108.3-108.4, 111.0, 113.9 and 205.0-206.5 s. Frame generation, snapshots and low latency
#   changed nothing. Draws can be dropped silently by: a render condition evaluated false on the CPU, no pipeline (DM_LIVE_SHADERS=skip, a failed build), a vertex or index
#   buffer the host finds in no pool, and others. Only one RED_ONCE line existed for any of them, and the game issuing no draw at all looked the same.
# WHAT IT CHANGES (dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m, hle_nvn.c; a test):
#   * g_draw_ops counts every draw record the replay meets (OP_DRAW, OP_DRAW_IDX, OP_MULTI_DRAW, OP_DRAW_TEX).
#   * drop_note counts each early return of the draw path by reason, 15 of them:
#     render_condition_false, no_program, raster_discard, diagnostic_switch, culled, empty_scissor, render_pass_not_begun, no_pipeline, vertex_buffer_not_in_pool,
#     arguments_ended_pass_twice, primitive_type, index_buffer_not_in_pool, past_multi_draw_count, mesh_or_wide_line_pipeline_missing, draw_texture_failed.
#     Logged at the first 4 cases and at powers of two, with what each saw:
#     - the pipeline's shader keys;
#     - the render condition's mode, address, values, and whether both were read from memory;
#     - the index range and the nearest pools, and whether a sparse pool holds an address that is in no pool (the vertex-stream line too).
#     Reasons the console shares are logged without [RED]. Render-enable conditions are counted evaluated true / false / unknown.
#   * stretch_note: 3 or more presents in a row whose frames encoded no draw give one "[RED] N presents in a row encoded no draw" line with the presents, the first frame, the
#     duration, the draw records replayed ("the game issued none" when 0), the drops by reason and the render conditions. First 16, then powers of two; also at 150 still going.
#     Every 300 presents: draw records, presents with no draw, drops by reason.
#   * Slow-frame rows: @draw_ops, @drops, @drop_why (bit i = reason i, in the order above).
#   * hud_layer: DM_METAL_HUD=1 sets the game layer's developerHUDProperties {mode: default, logging: default} once per layer, on the main thread, and logs it. Needed because
#     MTL_HUD_ENABLED only acts on a process's first Metal device. In GameApp that device is the app's own, made long before the game, and nothing translated DM_METAL_HUD.
#     Not with the Mac's front end, which has front_hud_env (g_hud_own).
# DEFAULT: all on (counters, a handful of log lines). No behaviour change for draws: the same draws are dropped as before, now counted.
# Reading the next log:
#   - "the game issued none" in the stretch lines: the game itself stopped drawing. Then look at what it waits on (sync waits, queries).
#   - "render_condition_false": the CPU-side render-condition evaluation (rc_value) is wrong for this game; its values and address are in the line.
#   - "no_pipeline": a missing / failed pipeline. Retry with DM_LIVE_SHADERS=pause; the keys tell which shader.
#   - "vertex_buffer_not_in_pool" / "index_buffer_not_in_pool": the nearest-pool distances tell a pool registered late or freed from a range overrun.
# Shader chain: not touched (b24b25240cad).
# Test: dm/gfx/tests/t_drop_reasons, 13 checks, 0 failed: the counters, a no-program draw through draw(), the stretch census, the HUD set once with mode default, and off with
#   DM_METAL_HUD=0. Rebuilt with 0506 + 0507 + 0508 on an M1 Pro: t_nvn 506/0, t_dead_targets 197/0, t_present_keep 10/0 + 10/0, t_vbuf_clamp 15/0 + 13/0,
#   t_addr_known 14/0, t_pool_chunks 178/0. NOT run on a device; no host dylib built.

# Rebased 2026-11-22 onto the new 0506 (upstream c96c45e9 + 79555b67 + the pool-end fallback): context only, same behaviour.

